<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  M365-Project : install-M365-Project.xml

  Project desktop app (Project Online Desktop Client, the desktop app that
  comes with Planner and Project Plan 3 or Planner and Project Plan 5). Add-on
  to an existing Microsoft 365 Apps installation. Company Portal available
  install.

  Worked example estate:
    The device already has Microsoft 365 Apps, installed by M365-Base or
    M365-Base-Business, on Monthly Enterprise Channel, 64-bit, en-us base
    language, possibly with da-dk added.

  No Channel attribute. No OfficeClientEdition attribute. Both omissions are
  deliberate and both are load bearing.

  Per the ODT reference on Microsoft Learn: if Microsoft 365 Apps is already
  installed and Channel is not specified, the ODT matches the channel of the
  existing installation, and the same applies to architecture when
  OfficeClientEdition is not specified.

  Hard-coding a channel here would re-channel the whole Office installation on
  any device that is not already on that channel, at the next update cycle
  rather than at install time. One user asking for Project should not move that
  device's Office to a different servicing channel. See MIGRATION.md, defect 2.

  Note the documented contradiction: the ODT configuration reference states
  that Channel is required alongside Version="MatchInstalled", while the
  Microsoft 365 Apps Rangers best practices page uses exactly this scenario as
  its worked example and omits Channel on purpose. This file follows the best
  practices page. Validate on a device that is not on Monthly Enterprise
  Channel before broad release. Full detail in README.md.

  Language matching. MatchInstalled with TargetProduct="All" gives Project the
  same languages already present across all installed products, and works
  whether the base is the enterprise or the business product ID.
-->
<Configuration ID="M365-Project">

  <Add Version="MatchInstalled" AllowCdnFallback="TRUE">
    <Product ID="ProjectProRetail">
      <Language ID="MatchInstalled" TargetProduct="All" />
    </Product>
  </Add>

  <Display Level="None" AcceptEULA="TRUE" />

  <Property Name="FORCEAPPSHUTDOWN" Value="FALSE" />

</Configuration>
